<div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30pt; padding-bottom: 16pt; border-bottom: 2pt solid #1e40af;">
    <h1 style="border-bottom: none; margin-bottom: 4pt; color: #1e3a8a;">ADAPTNET: ADAPTIVE NETWORK TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT</h1>
    <div style="font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 6pt;">
        Closed-Loop Traffic Orchestration via Machine Learning & Software-Defined Networking (SDN)
    </div>
    <div style="font-size: 10.5pt; color: #64748b;">
        Technical & Academic Project Report | Computer Networks Specialization
    </div>
</div>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>Executive Overview:</strong> AdaptNet is an intelligent, closed-loop network traffic management system bridging core Computer Networks fundamentals (OSI Layers 2–7, OpenFlow v1.3 SDN, TCP flow dynamics, Linux Traffic Control) with predictive Machine Learning (Random Forest Classification, K-Means Profiling, and Bidirectional GRU Congestion Forecasting).
</div>

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 1 -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>1. Problem Identification and Objective</h2>

<h3>1.1 Relevance to Computer Networks</h3>
<p>
    In packet-switched computer networks, traditional congestion management mechanisms operate almost entirely <strong>reactively</strong>. At the Transport Layer (Layer 4), algorithms such as TCP Reno, TCP Cubic, and BBR detect congestion only after queue buffers at intermediate switches have already filled up, leading to packet drops or substantial round-trip time (RTT) inflations. 
</p>
<p>
    Furthermore, switches and routers suffer from the pervasive <strong>Bufferbloat problem</strong>: oversized FIFO buffers introduce massive queueing delay without preventing tail drops during micro-bursts. Traditional Active Queue Management (AQM) techniques (e.g., RED, WRED, CoDel) operate blindly at the packet level, dropping or marking packets statistically without knowledge of the application context (e.g., treating low-latency VoIP or DNS packets identically to loss-resilient bulk downloads).
</p>

<h3>1.2 Core Project Objectives</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Sub-Second Network Telemetry:</strong> Continuously monitor and aggregate 5-tuple packet flows (Source IP, Destination IP, Source Port, Destination Port, Protocol) along with sliding window telemetry counters.</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-Class Traffic Categorization:</strong> Classify real-time flows into application categories (DNS, HTTP/Web, Video Streaming, SSH, Bulk Transfer, IoT/Other) with over 99% accuracy.</li>
    <li><strong>Host Behavioral Profiling:</strong> Cluster network edge nodes based on historical usage patterns (High-Throughput, Interactive Latency-Sensitive, Bulk, Idle) to prevent resource monopolization.</li>
    <li><strong>Proactive Congestion Forecasting:</strong> Utilize a Bidirectional Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) neural network over multi-timestep telemetry windows to forecast continuous congestion scores <code>[0.0, 1.0]</code> before buffer queues overflow.</li>
    <li><strong>Closed-Loop SDN Policy Enforcement:</strong> Automatically inject OpenFlow v1.3 flow modification (<code>FlowMod</code>) rules and adjust Linux Traffic Control (<code>tc</code>) Hierarchical Token Bucket (HTB) rate limiters in real time.</li>
    <li><strong>Explainable AI (XAI):</strong> Provide transparent, plain-English audit trails and SHAP feature attributions for every automated QoS throttling decision.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.3 Architectural Closed-Loop Control Flow Diagram</h3>
<div class="diagram-box">
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        ADAPTNET CLOSED-LOOP CONTROL PLANE                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                          |
                +-------------------------+-------------------------+
                |                                                   |
                v                                                   v
      +-------------------+                               +-------------------+
      |  Telemetry Input  |                               |   ML Analytics    |
