+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
</div>

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 2 -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>2. Network Topology Architecture and Protocols</h2>

<h3>2.1 Network Topology Details</h3>
<p>
    The primary testbed operates within a simulated <strong>5-Host Star / Dumbbell Bottleneck Topology</strong> implemented in Mininet, backed by an Open vSwitch (OVS) datapath and a Ryu OpenFlow Controller.
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>End-Hosts (h1 – h5):</strong> Configured on the <code>10.0.0.0/24</code> subnet (IPs: <code>10.0.0.1</code> to <code>10.0.0.5</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>OpenFlow Switch (s1):</strong> Managed via OpenFlow 1.3 protocol. Maintains independent meter bands and queueing handles.</li>
    <li><strong>Bottleneck Links:</strong> Edge links are configured with 100 Mbps bandwidth and 2 ms propagation delay. The internal switch forwarding queue is bounded to 50 packets to simulate real-world data center switch oversubscription.</li>
</ul>

<div class="diagram-box">
       [ Host h1 ] (10.0.0.1) ---- 100 Mbps, 2ms ----+
       [ Host h2 ] (10.0.0.2) ---- 100 Mbps, 2ms ----|
       [ Host h3 ] (10.0.0.3) ---- 100 Mbps, 2ms ----+--- [ OpenFlow Switch s1 ]
       [ Host h4 ] (10.0.0.4) ---- 100 Mbps, 2ms ----|     (Ryu Controller c0)
       [ Host h5 ] (10.0.0.5) ---- 100 Mbps, 2ms ----+
</div>

<h3>2.2 Protocols Employed Across OSI Layers</h3>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>OSI Layer</th>
            <th>Protocol</th>
            <th>Role & Function in AdaptNet</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 7 (Application)</strong></td>
            <td>HTTP / HTTPS</td>
            <td>Simulated web traffic, REST API communication between dashboard and Flask engine.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 7 (Application)</strong></td>
            <td>DNS (UDP/53)</td>
            <td>Domain name resolution benchmarking; designated as latency-critical high priority.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 7 (Application)</strong></td>
            <td>SSH (TCP/22)</td>
            <td>Interactive remote shell traffic; mapped to low-latency interactive priority.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 4 (Transport)</strong></td>
            <td>TCP</td>
            <td>Stateful 3-way handshake verification, sliding window telemetry, flag tracking (SYN/ACK/FIN).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 4 (Transport)</strong></td>
            <td>UDP</td>
            <td>Connectionless streaming traffic generation and stress-testing via <code>iperf3</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 3 (Network)</strong></td>
            <td>IPv4 / IPv6</td>
            <td>Packet addressing, routing, DiffServ DSCP header inspection and dynamic rewriting.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 3 (Network)</strong></td>
            <td>ICMP</td>
            <td>Ping telemetry for continuous end-to-end RTT sampling and loss detection.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Layer 2 (Data Link)</strong></td>
            <td>Ethernet (802.3) / ARP</td>
