        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>SDN Control Protocol</strong></td>
            <td>OpenFlow v1.3</td>
            <td>Controller-to-switch protocol for packet interception (<code>PacketIn</code>) and table flow installation (<code>FlowMod</code>).</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- SECTION 3 -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>3. Implementation and Functionalities</h2>

<h3>3.1 Six-Stage Continuous Pipeline</h3>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Wire Sniffing:</strong> Real-time capture of raw network frames using socket stream buffers and Scapy.</li>
    <li><strong>Flow Aggregator:</strong> Groups packets by 5-tuple key into bidirectional flow state records updated every 500 ms.</li>
    <li><strong>Traffic Classification (Random Forest):</strong> Predicts application class (<code>DNS</code>, <code>HTTP</code>, <code>VIDEO</code>, <code>SSH</code>, <code>BULK</code>, <code>OTHER</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Device Profiler (K-Means):</strong> Maps host telemetry vectors to dynamic behavioral personas (Clusters 0 to 3).</li>
    <li><strong>Congestion Forecaster (GRU):</strong> Predicts future congestion score <code>[0.0, 1.0]</code> over a 2-step sliding window.</li>
    <li><strong>Closed-Loop QoS Actuator:</strong> Re-marks IP DSCP headers and configures Linux Traffic Control HTB bandwidth queues.</li>
</ol>

<h3>3.2 Dynamic QoS Priority Matrix</h3>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Traffic Class</th>
            <th>Congestion State</th>
            <th>Host Persona</th>
            <th>Assigned Action</th>
            <th>DSCP Marking</th>
            <th>Bandwidth Queue</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>DNS / VoIP</td>
            <td>ANY</td>
            <td>ANY</td>
            <td><strong>HIGH (Guaranteed)</strong></td>
            <td>DSCP 46 (Expedited Forwarding)</td>
            <td>Queue 1:10 (Min 60 Mbps)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>SSH / Interactive</td>
            <td>LOW / MEDIUM</td>
            <td>Interactive</td>
            <td><strong>HIGH (Priority)</strong></td>
            <td>DSCP 34 (Assured Forwarding 41)</td>
            <td>Queue 1:10 (Min 60 Mbps)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>VIDEO Streaming</td>
            <td>LOW</td>
            <td>High-Throughput</td>
            <td><strong>NORMAL</strong></td>
            <td>DSCP 0 (Best Effort)</td>
            <td>Queue 1:20 (Min 30 Mbps)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>VIDEO Streaming</td>
            <td>HIGH (Score &ge; 0.67)</td>
            <td>High-Throughput</td>
            <td><strong>THROTTLE</strong></td>
            <td>DSCP 10 (Assured Forwarding 11)</td>
            <td>Queue 1:30 (Capped 10 Mbps)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>BULK / FTP / Backup</td>
            <td>MEDIUM</td>
            <td>Bulk Transfer</td>
            <td><strong>LOW</strong></td>
            <td>DSCP 8 (Class Selector 1)</td>
            <td>Queue 1:30 (Capped 10 Mbps)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>OTHER / Unclassified</td>
            <td>HIGH (Score &ge; 0.67)</td>
            <td>ANY</td>
            <td><strong>DROP / POLICE</strong></td>
            <td>Drop on queue threshold</td>
            <td>Drop tail / Meter rate drop</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

