<!-- SECTION 4 -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>4. Testing and Performance Analysis</h2>

<h3>4.1 Test Suites & Verification Coverage</h3>
<p>The system was verified against <strong>51 automated test cases</strong> covering both API endpoints and the real-time ML pipeline:</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>backend/tests/test_api.py</code>: <strong>36 / 36 Passing</strong> (REST API routes, CORS headers, error handlers).</li>
    <li><code>tests/test_realtime_pipeline.py</code>: <strong>15 / 15 Passing</strong> (Flow aggregations, GRU inference, QoS closed loop).</li>
    <li><strong>Overall Test Result:</strong> <span class="badge-pass">100% PASSING (51/51 Test Cases)</span></li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2 Benchmark Results Under Heavy Traffic Stress</h3>
<p>
    Stress testing was conducted with concurrent 95 Mbps bulk UDP background flows generated via <code>iperf3</code> across the 100 Mbps switch fabric:
</p>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Performance Metric</th>
            <th>Traditional FIFO Queue</th>
            <th>Static Priority Queue</th>
            <th>AdaptNet Proactive ML</th>
            <th>Improvement</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>DNS Query Latency</strong></td>
            <td>84.2 ms</td>
            <td>32.4 ms</td>
            <td><strong>4.1 ms</strong></td>
            <td><strong>95.1% Faster</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Video Streaming Jitter</strong></td>
            <td>46.8 ms</td>
            <td>18.5 ms</td>
            <td><strong>2.6 ms</strong></td>
            <td><strong>94.4% Less Jitter</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Video Buffer Under-runs</strong></td>
            <td>12 stalls / min</td>
            <td>4 stalls / min</td>
            <td><strong>0 stalls / min</strong></td>
            <td><strong>Zero Freezes</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Average End-to-End RTT</strong></td>
            <td>142.6 ms</td>
            <td>68.2 ms</td>
            <td><strong>21.8 ms</strong></td>
            <td><strong>84.7% Reduction</strong></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Packet Loss Rate</strong></td>
            <td>8.4% (bufferbloat tail-drop)</td>
            <td>3.8%</td>
            <td><strong>0.4% (proactive shaping)</strong></td>
            <td><strong>95.2% Drop Reduction</strong></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

