<!-- SECTION 5 -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>5. Application and Practical Relevance</h2>

<h3>5.1 Real-World Industrial & Commercial Applications</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>5G / 6G Network Slicing:</strong> Dynamically guarantees ultra-low latency slices for autonomous vehicular signaling (uRLLC) while isolating high-throughput media consumers (eMBB).</li>
    <li><strong>Data Center Incast Mitigation:</strong> Proactively throttles non-urgent worker responses to prevent switch buffer exhaustion during partition-aggregate queries (e.g., in MapReduce and database clustering).</li>
    <li><strong>Enterprise SD-WAN Gateways:</strong> Protects mission-critical video conferences and cloud ERP sessions over congested public broadband uplinks.</li>
</ul>

<h3>5.2 Computer Networks Knowledge Integration</h3>
<p>
    AdaptNet directly realizes textbook networking principles in live working software:
</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Layer 2/3:</strong> Ethernet framing, ARP caching, IP header parsing, and DiffServ DSCP field rewriting.</li>
    <li><strong>Layer 4:</strong> TCP state machine tracking, 3-way handshake verification, sliding window telemetry, and flow-level rate shaping.</li>
    <li><strong>SDN Paradigm:</strong> Decoupled Control Plane orchestrating a lightweight Data Plane via OpenFlow v1.3.</li>
    <li><strong>Queueing Disciplines:</strong> Hierarchical Token Bucket (HTB) rate enforcement and Fair Queueing with Controlled Delay (CoDel).</li>
</ul>

